{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490814-rouse-spirit-create-genius-loci","id":1490814,"title":"Rouse Spirit / Create Genius Loci","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-20T15:34:23-07:00","id":1490814,"title":"Rouse Spirit / Create Genius Loci","content":"MtA 1st ed. had a Rouse Spirit spell that was like a supercharged coax spell, and would let you basically awaken the spirit of a house, rock, what have you, effectively creating a rank 1 spirit. Rouse spirit in MtA 2e simply serves to awaken already extant spirits which have gone dormant.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to, say, rouse the spirit of my new Sanctum to act as an ally / genius loci (assuming that there was not an already extant spirit there that had been put into dormancy) how would I do it? Coax, then bolster spirit with advanced duration while trying to discover how long before it can become an active spirit of it's own? Are there any rules for this, or would this be a mystery with which to contend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T15:45:45-07:00","id":1490817,"title":"","content":"I'd rule that you can use the coax-and-bolster method, then encourage the entity to feed and grow. It becomes &quot;Permenant&quot; when the character puts xp into an appropriate Merit - Ally, Familiar, Safe Place, etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T16:14:36-07:00","id":1490818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490814-rouse-spirit-create-genius-loci?p=1490817#post1490817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rule that you can use the coax-and-bolster method, then encourage the entity to feed and grow. It becomes &quot;Permenant&quot; when the character puts xp into an appropriate Merit - Ally, Familiar, Safe Place, etc</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, that seems workable. I guess I could designate one dot of the &quot;safe place&quot; merit as for the genius loci rather than a trap.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T16:27:37-07:00","id":1490821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490814-rouse-spirit-create-genius-loci?p=1490818#post1490818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you, that seems workable. I guess I could designate one dot of the &amp;quot;safe place&amp;quot; merit as for the genius loci rather than a trap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know a huge amount about Genius Loci in Mage, but couldn't it be a sentient part of the defenses? Like the house in <i>Monster House</i>, or The House from <i>House of Blades</i>? So it would still be a &quot;trap&quot;, just one facilitated by the spirit of the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T16:29:16-07:00","id":1490822,"title":"","content":"Another option is to make a Supernal summoning of a household Totem. Have them tutor the mage about aligning the Sanctum's feng shui to more efficiently generate a Genius Loci, or incentivize it via the Resonance of any passing ley lines. <br /> <br /> A summoning area for such a Totem would probably be easy to hide and comfortable. Its possible continually exposure to its Supernal power might hasten the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-20-2022, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T16:37:25-07:00","id":1490824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490814-rouse-spirit-create-genius-loci?p=1490822#post1490822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option is to make a Supernal summoning of a household Totem. Have them tutor the mage about aligning the Sanctum's feng shui to more efficiently generate a Genius Loci, or incentivize it via the Resonance of any passing ley lines. <br /> <br /> A summoning area for such a Totem would probably be easy to hide and comfortable. Its possible continually exposure to its Supernal power might hasten the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening a spirit of the Mage's choice also seems like a decent Boon for a Spirit-aspected Supernal Entity. The flavor of it might shift depending on the type - one woken by a Wraith would be more unwelcoming of intruders, while a Fae might birth one that adheres strictly to rules of hospitality<br /> <br /> There's already precedent in that a Demon can temporarily raise an Ephemeral Entity to human-level sapience","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-20-2022, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T17:15:36-07:00","id":1490826,"title":"","content":"I think the intent of the summoner would also inform it. A Wraith could make a house be unwelcoming to intruders, but could make it a place to mentally heal, gain good counsel or self reflect.<br /> <br /> A Specter could make a home be deadly to invaders, but could also make it a good place to remember heartfelt memories of those the dwellers lost.<br /> <br /> A Cherubim could make a house be a place where lies tend to be found out easier or could make them places that Resonate with creativity and inspiration, perfect for writers, architects and more.<br /> <br /> A Moirae could design it so that thieves and other with hostile intent would stumble into unlucky coincidences (trapped under a bookshelf, placed hand on a hot stove, neighbors call the police, etc), just as much as they can make it a place that feels welcoming and homely to those that are gracious guests.<br /> <br /> A Totem would probably help the mage create a home akin to the one in The Ancient Magus' Bride, not only helping in awakening it, but drawing spirits that would fit its theme to the mage. I can also see it being the case for Moirae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T17:23:44-07:00","id":1490827,"title":"","content":"I've never really done any supernal summonings in my game, but it is an interesting option. The character in question is an acanthus this so it would have to be some sort of fae, but I could just summon a fae with some influence in spirit. Thank you for the ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T17:43:35-07:00","id":1490828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490814-rouse-spirit-create-genius-loci#post1490814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MtA 1st ed. had a Rouse Spirit spell that was like a supercharged coax spell, and would let you basically awaken the spirit of a house, rock, what have you, effectively creating a rank 1 spirit. Rouse spirit in MtA 2e simply serves to awaken already extant spirits which have gone dormant.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are the same phenomenon, distinguished solely by whether one has awakened before or not. If a spirit's been around long enough to reach Rank 1 you would just cast Rouse Spirit on it as normal and the spirit would lose 1 Essence as it wakes up for the first time.<br /> <br /> Werewolf 2e core gives an example of the sorts of phenomena that can awaken a dormant spirit on page 183, as well as noting that simply surviving for long enough is sufficient for a spirit to reach Rank 1 and become rousable.<br /> <br /> Unless you're looking at an extremely and completely new structure on land where nothing previously existed, there is probably something around that can do the job of being &quot;the spirit of your Sanctum.&quot; (Genius loci are not spirits in the conventional sense \u2014 they wouldn't be on the Incomplete List of Weird Stuff if it were that simple.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T18:12:40-07:00","id":1490833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490814-rouse-spirit-create-genius-loci?p=1490828#post1490828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Genius loci are not spirits in the conventional sense \u2014 they wouldn't be on the Incomplete List of Weird Stuff if it were that simple.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Time to break out the high-Scale Golem spells. Bonus points of it has the Mind/Death/Spirit enhancement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T00:00:22-07:00","id":1490848,"title":"","content":"Just a note, i don't think a genius loci is a spirit. It is a place with a mind... Not a place effectively possessed by a spirit. <br /> <br /> Golem+mind 5 would i think model it better. Of course if you just want an intelligence, the Spirit works fine. You could also use a ghost.<br /> <br /> Edit: it is supposed to he a mystery, not, oh look a spirit, call the thyrsus/local pack.<br /> <br /> Also, the ghost of a building would be cool. Hard to get them sentient though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-21-2022, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T05:36:04-07:00","id":1490867,"title":"","content":"I had been under an assumption that Genii Loci were just the spirits of places (houses, forests, meadows) as opposed to things (rocks, trees, well-loved cars). I had apparently forgotten about the &quot;weird stuff&quot; list from the core book. Thanks to those of you who reminded me. The info on rousing a spirit is still usefull, but now I am going to look into what a Genius Luci may actually be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 08-21-2022, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T05:55:55-07:00","id":1490868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490814-rouse-spirit-create-genius-loci?p=1490848#post1490848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a note, i don't think a genius loci is a spirit. It is a place with a mind... Not a place effectively possessed by a spirit.<br /> <br /> Golem+mind 5 would i think model it better. Of course if you just want an intelligence, the Spirit works fine. You could also use a ghost.<br /> <br /> Edit: it is supposed to he a mystery, not, oh look a spirit, call the thyrsus/local pack.<br /> <br /> Also, the ghost of a building would be cool. Hard to get them sentient though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To my understanding, if there is a ghost of a building, then the actual building must have been destroyed, so you can't use it as a sanctum.<br /> <br /> But now I do wonder how workable it would be to use Ghost gate to enter twilight and use the ghost building as a sanctum. Would it effectively work like a real building while the characters are in twilight? What about plumbing?<br /> <br /> It would certainly up the security regarding most parties.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T06:26:43-07:00","id":1490875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490814-rouse-spirit-create-genius-loci?p=1490868#post1490868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To my understanding, if there is a ghost of a building, then the actual building must have been destroyed, so you can't use it as a sanctum.<br /> <br /> But now I do wonder how workable it would be to use Ghost gate to enter twilight and use the ghost building as a sanctum. Would it effectively work like a real building while the characters are in twilight? What about plumbing?<br /> <br /> It would certainly up the security regarding most parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could destroy the building to create a ghost, and then rebuilding, the issue is that it starts out as a rank 0 by default, unless the creation of the ghost caused integrity loss/breaking point (i think). And unlike spirits, ghost typically don't increase in rank without going to the underworld... <br /> <br /> Still, a ghost building in twilight would still be a ghost (rank 0 by default). It would have anchors, and be at risk of being dragged into the underworld. But with a little bit of magic that should be fairly easy to prevent. <br /> <br /> Aside, I'm not sure if you need plumbing while in twilight, going into death/spirit twilight transforms your body i to death/spirit attuned ephemera (mind projections leave your body behind and create a dream form).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T09:52:45-07:00","id":1490887,"title":"","content":"That sounds more like the <i>Spirit Manse</i> spell, maybe an equivalent with Death Twilight could be done as well, granting Safe Place for Sanctum security.<br /> <br /> Another option is to cultivate guardians. In the Voice of Freedom AP (a great story and easy recommendation), the cabal made their sanctum Resonant to a flock of drone spirits and then bought some foo dog statues. They turned out to house some Rank 3 spirits that agreed to guard the Sanctum for some incense offerings. The spirits had golden claws, intense eyes and were sparse with words, and they did their job well, but were scary nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Spirit mages can end up making some weird decoration choices or pick up some odd habits, sticking to both with dogged determination. But its because they know the old ways, they listen to voices beyond the material and these forces guard them in return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-21-2022, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T21:23:24-07:00","id":1490965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490814-rouse-spirit-create-genius-loci?p=1490887#post1490887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> Another option is to cultivate guardians. In the Voice of Freedom AP (a great story and easy recommendation), the cabal made their sanctum Resonant to a flock of drone spirits and then bought some foo dog statues. They turned out to house some Rank 3 spirits that agreed to guard the Sanctum for some incense offerings. The spirits had golden claws, intense eyes and were sparse with words, and they did their job well, but were scary nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Spirit mages can end up making some weird decoration choices or pick up some odd habits, sticking to both with dogged determination. But its because they know the old ways, they listen to voices beyond the material and these forces guard them in return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feng Shui yourself a Three Dog Knight. There's plenty of potential in using <i>S\u00ec Xi\u00e0ng </i>to generate a mini spirit court in your house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}